<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">I / The name</span>
      <h2>The line a system turns on.</h2>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body" data-reveal>
      <p>
        A-XS is a contraction of <em>axis</em>: the line a system turns on. The hyphen
        is that line. It is a useful constraint for a studio — every project should have
        an axis, a central decision that everything else is measured against.
      </p>
      <p>
        The mark is a compass rose reduced to its essentials: a ring, a cross, a diamond,
        four copper nodes. It is drawn, not decorated. The same logic applies to the
        software.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        “The work should hold under inspection.”
        <cite>A-XS / studio note</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">II / Why private</span>
      <h2>The archive is closed because the work is not finished.</h2>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Unfinished work should not be presented as a product. Screenshots, download
        counts, and launch pages are easy to manufacture; a system that holds under
        inspection is not. The current body of work is in development and stays private
        until it meets that bar.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not mystique. It is a standard. When a project is ready, it will be
        documented here with its architecture, measurements, and limits. Until then,
        private dossiers are available on request for serious conversations.
      </p>
      <div class="access-panel__actions">
        <a class="button button--accent" href="/archive/">About the archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Request a dossier <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

